BUILT. `draco.draketarget.RuleAspectText` (from Surface) owns the LAYOUT: parameters `variables`, `conditions` and
`action` as already-rendered lines and `present` (default true); the `rule` head, `pattern` with its `variables` and
`conditions` blocks, `action` with its body, each block elided when empty — a present rule with nothing in it is the
one line `rule`, an absent one renders nothing and, the arguments being by-name behind `guard(_present)`, evaluates
nothing. `draco.gendrake.RuleAspectOf` (from RuleAspectText) is the MAPPING from a TypeDefinition: presence read with
`fold`, the pattern's variables and conditions rendered at level 3 and the action's body at level 2 through
`elementText ((TypeElement, Int) -> [Text])`, the same explicit dependency DracoAspectOf receives, so the generated
main types never call the mods engine. DrakeTarget and GenDrake list the two. `Drake.emit` delegates through a new
`private[draco] ruleAspectText(td)`, beside `dracoAspectText`; its hand-written block is gone. Four JSON are
`DrakeCLI parse` of their surfaces, four Scala `GeneratorCLI generate`, the emitter recompiled against them; with the
new emitter `DrakeCLI check` reads surface drift 0, json drift 0 over main and mods — every surface byte-identical.
